From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: apple-sio: leave the T8132 stop to the
 sleep's commit

On T8132 the SIO driver stops its firmware itself in .suspend. The
sleep controller's last check then has no CPU control window for it,
as only a coprocessor registered for the commit gives it one, and
counts the SIO as running. Every deep sleep is refused:

  apple-sleep 380700000.sleep-controller: dma-controller didn't stop:
  control 0x0 status 0x0
  apple-sleep 380700000.sleep-controller: refused: 1 coprocessors that
  must stop or gate are still running

The stop it did is not undone by the refusal either. The firmware
does not come back without a real sleep, and the SIO stays stopped:

  apple-sio 3ade00000.dma-controller: sleep refused: firmware not back
  after a reset (-19), stopped until a real sleep

Leave the stop to the commit, as on T8140: the driver registers its
ASC with the sleep controller, which then sees it ready, and a sleep
refused before the commit leaves the firmware running.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/dma/apple-sio.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c b/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c
index 56576bc193..5af7b41bcc 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/apple-sio.c
@@ -648,6 +648,8 @@ static const struct sio_hw_data sio_hw_t6030 = {
  * threshold 0x800.
  */
 static const struct sio_hw_data sio_hw_t8132 = {
+	/* Stopped by its driver, it does not come back from a sleep refused later. */
+	.stop_at_commit = true,
 	.protocol = 10,
 	.fifo_threshold = 0x800,
 	.cfg_word4 = 0x800,
-- 
